{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": "before", "result": {}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 0, "result": {"protocolVersion": "2025-06-18", "capabilities": {"tools": {"listChanged": false}, "resources": {}, "prompts": {}}, "serverInfo": {"name": "ucas", "title": "ucas, a computer algebra system for programmers", "version": "1"}, "instructions": "ucas analyses functions (exhaustively on machine types), does exact algebra and calculus, transforms, number theory and finite fields, and finds cheaper implementations, each answer checked or proved.  Expressions are ucas syntax strings; give parameters types (x: u8, x: f32, x: real) where it matters.  Definitions persist across calls.  An ambiguous input is an error listing its readings: retry with args.assume.KEY.  structuredContent holds the typed result, checks and proof."}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 1, "result": {}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 2, "result": {"tools": [{"name": "analyze", "title": "Analyse a function", "description": "Exhaustive or sampled analysis of a function over its domain (machine types u8..u64, i8..i64, f16, f32, f64, real, int): values, range, where it is defined, wrapping and C UB, critical points, equivalence of two functions (with a counterexample), error and fit of an approximation, cost under a GPU cost model, the graphics fixed-function states (blending, logic ops, stencil) that compute a scatter's update, minimal gate networks (with a proof of minimality), cheaper equivalent implementations, polynomial/rational approximations.\n\nCall with {\"op\": OP, \"args\": {...}}; expressions are ucas syntax strings (x^2 sin(x), isqrt(x: u4)) or an AST ({\"op\": \"+\", \"args\": [...]}).  Ops (* = required arg):\n- show(f*): the function, typed\n- table(f*, max): values at the points of the domain\n- parse(expr*): the expression fully parenthesised\n- range(f*, nocrit): min/max over the domain\n- domain(f*): the conditions of the partial operations and the inputs where F is defined\n- wrap(f*): nuw/nsw per operation, C UB, end-to-end agreement with the mathematical result\n- crit(f*): critical points, extrema, inflection points\n- equiv(f*, g*, ftz, nanbits): equal on F's domain? (with a counterexample)\n- fit(g*, f*, metric): choose G's extra parameters to approximate F\n- error(g*, f*): error of G as an approximation of F\n- cost(f*, model, consecutive): price under a cost model\n- rop(f*, model): graphics fixed-function states (blending, logic ops, stencil) that compute a per-cell update F(s, d), each proved and priced\n- gates(f*, basis, max, nodes, as_c): minimal gate network, with proof\n- find(f*, n, max): cheaper implementations under the cost model\n- more(n): the next results of the last find\n- approx(f*, in, options): polynomial/rational approximations, measured\n- approx_more(n): more candidates of the last approx\n- dword(f*, tol, atol, ulp, model): f64 arithmetic over f32 (alone, or as double-word pairs) where the model prices that lower, with a derived error bound and its conditions\n- foldproof(f*, model): the float round trips the model's driver folds, and their rounding as integer arithmetic it cannot fold, proved equal\n- banks(accesses*, size, elem, model): the bank-conflict degree of shared-memory index expressions over a warp, and a proved index swizzle that lowers it when the model prices conflicts\n- intatomic(f*, count, tol, global, model): a float atomic add as an integer atomic add on fixed point, when its values are proved exact there (or within tol) and the model prices it lower\n- stoke(f*, steps, restarts, len, seed, model): MCMC (Metropolis-Hastings) over straight-line integer programs priced by the model; what reaches distance 0 is verified on the whole domain\n- pit(f*, g*, trials, seed): polynomial identity testing (Schwartz-Zippel): a probabilistic answer with its error bound\n- phash(f*, seed, model): a switch's keys hashed injectively into a table, when the model prices the lookup below the compare chain\nEvery op also takes assume (answers to ambiguities, from an error's readings), defaults, timeout_s, files.  Example: {\"op\": \"show\", \"args\": {\"f\": \"x^3 - 3x\"}}", "inputSchema": {"type": "object", "properties": {"op": {"type": "string", "enum": ["show", "table", "parse", "range", "domain", "wrap", "crit", "equiv", "fit", "error", "cost", "rop", "gates", "find", "more", "approx", "approx_more", "dword", "foldproof", "banks", "intatomic", "stoke", "pit", "phash"], "description": "the operation"}, "args": {"type": "object", "description": "the op's named arguments (see the description; the exact schema of each op is in the session tool's schema op)"}}, "required": ["op"], "additionalProperties": false}, "outputSchema": {"type": "object", "required": ["id", "ok", "cmd"], "properties": {"id": {"description": "the request's id, as given (null if none)"}, "ok": {"type": "boolean"}, "cmd": {"type": ["string", "null"]}, "ucas": {"description": "the ucas statements that ran (error positions refer to them)", "type": "string"}, "structured": {"description": "result has fields beyond text", "type": "boolean"}, "result": {"description": "the command's fields (kind, ...); exact values as {value, exact}; expressions as ucas strings that parse back; unstructured commands give {text}", "type": "object"}, "results": {"description": "every result, when the request ran several commands", "type": "array"}, "notes": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"enum": ["rule", "info", "assumed", "default"]}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}}, "conditions": {"description": "where the answer holds", "type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}}, "checks": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"type": "string"}, "points": {"type": "integer"}, "max_diff": {"type": "number"}, "passed": {"type": "boolean"}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}}, "proof": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"enum": ["symbolic", "exhaustive", "sat", "numeric", "search"]}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}, "files": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"name": {"type": "string"}, "mime": {"type": "string"}, "bytes": {"type": "integer"}, "path": {"type": "string"}, "base64": {"type": "string"}}}}, "text": {"description": "the output as the CLI prints it", "type": "string"}, "error": {"type": "object", "required": ["code", "message"], "properties": {"code": {"enum": ["bad_json", "bad_request", "unknown_command", "parse_error", "domain_error", "unsupported", "failed", "ambiguous", "needs_input", "not_understood", "timeout", "internal"]}, "message": {"type": "string"}, "pos": {"type": "object", "properties": {"line": {"type": "integer"}, "col": {"type": "integer"}}}, "key": {"description": "ambiguous: the args.assume key that picks a reading", "type": "string"}, "readings": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"index": {"type": "integer"}, "reading": {"type": "string"}, "default": {"type": "boolean"}, "how": {"type": "string"}}}}, "how": {"type": "string"}}}}}}, {"name": "calculus", "title": "Calculus", "description": "Derivatives (higher, partial, mixed), gradient, Hessian, Laplacian, Jacobian, Wronskian, limits (symbolic and numeric), Taylor series, implicit derivatives, integrals (antiderivative checked by differentiating back; definite also numerically; contour integrals with around), closed forms of sums and loops, evaluation schemes, ODEs.\n\nCall with {\"op\": OP, \"args\": {...}}; expressions are ucas syntax strings (x^2 sin(x), isqrt(x: u4)) or an AST ({\"op\": \"+\", \"args\": [...]}).  Ops (* = required arg):\n- diff(f*, vars, order): derivative (higher, partial, mixed)\n- grad(f*, at): the gradient\n- hessian(f*, at): the Hessian (and at a point the second-derivative test)\n- laplacian(f*, at): the Laplacian\n- jacobian(fs*, wrt, at): the Jacobian matrix\n- wronskian(fs*, var): the Wronskian and linear independence\n- limit(f*, var, to*, side): a limit, symbolically and numerically\n- taylor(f*, var, at, order): Taylor polynomial, checked\n- implicit(equation*, for, wrt, order): dy/dx of an implicit curve\n- integrate(f*, var, from, to, around, qmc, points, replicates, seed, owen): antiderivative (checked by differentiating back) or definite integral\n- antiderivative(f*, var): an antiderivative + C\n- closed(f*): closed forms of sums, products, loops\n- scheme(f*, more, model): evaluation schemes priced\n- continuous(f*): sums as integrals, loops as ODEs\n- dsolve(name*, from, to, steps): solve a defined ODE (symbolic or numeric)\nEvery op also takes assume (answers to ambiguities, from an error's readings), defaults, timeout_s, files.  Example: {\"op\": \"diff\", \"args\": {\"f\": \"x^3 - 3x\"}}", "inputSchema": {"type": "object", "properties": {"op": {"type": "string", "enum": ["diff", "grad", "hessian", "laplacian", "jacobian", "wronskian", "limit", "taylor", "implicit", "integrate", "antiderivative", "closed", "scheme", "continuous", "dsolve"], "description": "the operation"}, "args": {"type": "object", "description": "the op's named arguments (see the description; the exact schema of each op is in the session tool's schema op)"}}, "required": ["op"], "additionalProperties": false}, "outputSchema": {"type": "object", "required": ["id", "ok", "cmd"], "properties": {"id": {"description": "the request's id, as given (null if none)"}, "ok": {"type": "boolean"}, "cmd": {"type": ["string", "null"]}, "ucas": {"description": "the ucas statements that ran (error positions refer to them)", "type": "string"}, "structured": {"description": "result has fields beyond text", "type": "boolean"}, "result": {"description": "the command's fields (kind, ...); exact values as {value, exact}; expressions as ucas strings that parse back; unstructured commands give {text}", "type": "object"}, "results": {"description": "every result, when the request ran several commands", "type": "array"}, "notes": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"enum": ["rule", "info", "assumed", "default"]}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}}, "conditions": {"description": "where the answer holds", "type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}}, "checks": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"type": "string"}, "points": {"type": "integer"}, "max_diff": {"type": "number"}, "passed": {"type": "boolean"}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}}, "proof": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"enum": ["symbolic", "exhaustive", "sat", "numeric", "search"]}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}, "files": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"name": {"type": "string"}, "mime": {"type": "string"}, "bytes": {"type": "integer"}, "path": {"type": "string"}, "base64": {"type": "string"}}}}, "text": {"description": "the output as the CLI prints it", "type": "string"}, "error": {"type": "object", "required": ["code", "message"], "properties": {"code": {"enum": ["bad_json", "bad_request", "unknown_command", "parse_error", "domain_error", "unsupported", "failed", "ambiguous", "needs_input", "not_understood", "timeout", "internal"]}, "message": {"type": "string"}, "pos": {"type": "object", "properties": {"line": {"type": "integer"}, "col": {"type": "integer"}}}, "key": {"description": "ambiguous: the args.assume key that picks a reading", "type": "string"}, "readings": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"index": {"type": "integer"}, "reading": {"type": "string"}, "default": {"type": "boolean"}, "how": {"type": "string"}}}}, "how": {"type": "string"}}}}}}, {"name": "algebra", "title": "Symbolic algebra", "description": "Polynomials and rational functions over Q, exactly: expand, factor, simplify (conditions where a factor cancelled), partial fractions, gcd/lcm, resultants, discriminants, division, solving equations and systems (every solution substituted back), substitution.\n\nCall with {\"op\": OP, \"args\": {...}}; expressions are ucas syntax strings (x^2 sin(x), isqrt(x: u4)) or an AST ({\"op\": \"+\", \"args\": [...]}).  Ops (* = required arg):\n- expand(f*): expanded over Q\n- factor(f*): factored over Q\n- simplify(f*): the simplest normal form\n- together(f*): one fraction\n- cancel(f*): common factors cancelled\n- collect(f*, var): collected in a variable\n- apart(f*, var): partial fractions\n- gcd(p*, q*): polynomial gcd\n- lcm(p*, q*): polynomial lcm\n- resultant(p*, q*, var): the resultant\n- discriminant(p*, var): the discriminant\n- quo(p*, q*, var): polynomial quotient\n- rem(p*, q*, var): polynomial remainder\n- divide(p*, q*, var): division with remainder\n- solve(equations*, for): equations and systems, every solution substituted back\n- substitute(values*, f*): F at values\nEvery op also takes assume (answers to ambiguities, from an error's readings), defaults, timeout_s, files.  Example: {\"op\": \"expand\", \"args\": {\"f\": \"x^3 - 3x\"}}", "inputSchema": {"type": "object", "properties": {"op": {"type": "string", "enum": ["expand", "factor", "simplify", "together", "cancel", "collect", "apart", "gcd", "lcm", "resultant", "discriminant", "quo", "rem", "divide", "solve", "substitute"], "description": "the operation"}, "args": {"type": "object", "description": "the op's named arguments (see the description; the exact schema of each op is in the session tool's schema op)"}}, "required": ["op"], "additionalProperties": false}, "outputSchema": {"type": "object", "required": ["id", "ok", "cmd"], "properties": {"id": {"description": "the request's id, as given (null if none)"}, "ok": {"type": "boolean"}, "cmd": {"type": ["string", "null"]}, "ucas": {"description": "the ucas statements that ran (error positions refer to them)", "type": "string"}, "structured": {"description": "result has fields beyond text", "type": "boolean"}, "result": {"description": "the command's fields (kind, ...); exact values as {value, exact}; expressions as ucas strings that parse back; unstructured commands give {text}", "type": "object"}, "results": {"description": "every result, when the request ran several commands", "type": "array"}, "notes": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"enum": ["rule", "info", "assumed", "default"]}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}}, "conditions": {"description": "where the answer holds", "type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}}, "checks": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"type": "string"}, "points": {"type": "integer"}, "max_diff": {"type": "number"}, "passed": {"type": "boolean"}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}}, "proof": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"enum": ["symbolic", "exhaustive", "sat", "numeric", "search"]}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}, "files": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"name": {"type": "string"}, "mime": {"type": "string"}, "bytes": {"type": "integer"}, "path": {"type": "string"}, "base64": {"type": "string"}}}}, "text": {"description": "the output as the CLI prints it", "type": "string"}, "error": {"type": "object", "required": ["code", "message"], "properties": {"code": {"enum": ["bad_json", "bad_request", "unknown_command", "parse_error", "domain_error", "unsupported", "failed", "ambiguous", "needs_input", "not_understood", "timeout", "internal"]}, "message": {"type": "string"}, "pos": {"type": "object", "properties": {"line": {"type": "integer"}, "col": {"type": "integer"}}}, "key": {"description": "ambiguous: the args.assume key that picks a reading", "type": "string"}, "readings": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"index": {"type": "integer"}, "reading": {"type": "string"}, "default": {"type": "boolean"}, "how": {"type": "string"}}}}, "how": {"type": "string"}}}}}}, {"name": "properties", "title": "Properties of a function", "description": "Monotonicity, period, classification (identify: polynomials, conics, ODEs ...), zeros, parity, symmetry, bounds, injective/surjective/bijective, continuity, convexity, asymptotes; each tagged proved, exhaustive or numeric.\n\nCall with {\"op\": OP, \"args\": {...}}; expressions are ucas syntax strings (x^2 sin(x), isqrt(x: u4)) or an AST ({\"op\": \"+\", \"args\": [...]}).  Ops (* = required arg):\n- monotonic(f*, var, in): increasing/decreasing, intervals\n- period(f*, var): the fundamental period\n- identify(f*): classify an expression, equation, conic or ODE\n- zeros(f*): the zeros (exact for polynomials)\n- parity(f*): even/odd, symmetries\n- symmetry(f*): axes x = c, centres, f(x, y) = f(y, x)\n- bounded(f*): bounds, poles, growth\n- injective(f*): one to one? (with a witness)\n- surjective(f*, onto): onto? (with a value never taken)\n- bijective(f*): a bijection?\n- continuity(f*): discontinuities by kind\n- convexity(f*): convex/concave intervals\n- asymptotes(f*): vertical, horizontal, oblique\nEvery op also takes assume (answers to ambiguities, from an error's readings), defaults, timeout_s, files.  Example: {\"op\": \"monotonic\", \"args\": {\"f\": \"x^3 - 3x\"}}", "inputSchema": {"type": "object", "properties": {"op": {"type": "string", "enum": ["monotonic", "period", "identify", "zeros", "parity", "symmetry", "bounded", "injective", "surjective", "bijective", "continuity", "convexity", "asymptotes"], "description": "the operation"}, "args": {"type": "object", "description": "the op's named arguments (see the description; the exact schema of each op is in the session tool's schema op)"}}, "required": ["op"], "additionalProperties": false}, "outputSchema": {"type": "object", "required": ["id", "ok", "cmd"], "properties": {"id": {"description": "the request's id, as given (null if none)"}, "ok": {"type": "boolean"}, "cmd": {"type": ["string", "null"]}, "ucas": {"description": "the ucas statements that ran (error positions refer to them)", "type": "string"}, "structured": {"description": "result has fields beyond text", "type": "boolean"}, "result": {"description": "the command's fields (kind, ...); exact values as {value, exact}; expressions as ucas strings that parse back; unstructured commands give {text}", "type": "object"}, "results": {"description": "every result, when the request ran several commands", "type": "array"}, "notes": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"enum": ["rule", "info", "assumed", "default"]}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}}, "conditions": {"description": "where the answer holds", "type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}}, "checks": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"type": "string"}, "points": {"type": "integer"}, "max_diff": {"type": "number"}, "passed": {"type": "boolean"}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}}, "proof": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"enum": ["symbolic", "exhaustive", "sat", "numeric", "search"]}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}, "files": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"name": {"type": "string"}, "mime": {"type": "string"}, "bytes": {"type": "integer"}, "path": {"type": "string"}, "base64": {"type": "string"}}}}, "text": {"description": "the output as the CLI prints it", "type": "string"}, "error": {"type": "object", "required": ["code", "message"], "properties": {"code": {"enum": ["bad_json", "bad_request", "unknown_command", "parse_error", "domain_error", "unsupported", "failed", "ambiguous", "needs_input", "not_understood", "timeout", "internal"]}, "message": {"type": "string"}, "pos": {"type": "object", "properties": {"line": {"type": "integer"}, "col": {"type": "integer"}}}, "key": {"description": "ambiguous: the args.assume key that picks a reading", "type": "string"}, "readings": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"index": {"type": "integer"}, "reading": {"type": "string"}, "default": {"type": "boolean"}, "how": {"type": "string"}}}}, "how": {"type": "string"}}}}}}, {"name": "complex", "title": "Complex numbers", "description": "Complex numbers and functions: a + bi forms, polar form, real/imaginary parts, trigonometric rewrites (each checked), n-th roots, holomorphy (Cauchy-Riemann), residues, poles.  z and w are complex variables (args.assume.z = \"complex\").\n\nCall with {\"op\": OP, \"args\": {...}}; expressions are ucas syntax strings (x^2 sin(x), isqrt(x: u4)) or an AST ({\"op\": \"+\", \"args\": [...]}).  Ops (* = required arg):\n- complex(f*): as a + bi\n- re(f*): the real part\n- im(f*): the imaginary part\n- conj(f*): the conjugate\n- modulus(f*): the modulus\n- arg(f*): the argument\n- polar(f*): r e^(i theta)\n- trig(f*, mode): equivalent trig forms\n- nthroots(n*, f*): the N complex N-th roots\n- unity(n*): the N-th roots of unity\n- holomorphic(f*): Cauchy-Riemann; the complex derivative\n- residue(f*, at*): the residue at a point\n- poles(f*): the poles and their orders\nEvery op also takes assume (answers to ambiguities, from an error's readings), defaults, timeout_s, files.  Example: {\"op\": \"complex\", \"args\": {\"f\": \"x^3 - 3x\"}}", "inputSchema": {"type": "object", "properties": {"op": {"type": "string", "enum": ["complex", "re", "im", "conj", "modulus", "arg", "polar", "trig", "nthroots", "unity", "holomorphic", "residue", "poles"], "description": "the operation"}, "args": {"type": "object", "description": "the op's named arguments (see the description; the exact schema of each op is in the session tool's schema op)"}}, "required": ["op"], "additionalProperties": false}, "outputSchema": {"type": "object", "required": ["id", "ok", "cmd"], "properties": {"id": {"description": "the request's id, as given (null if none)"}, "ok": {"type": "boolean"}, "cmd": {"type": ["string", "null"]}, "ucas": {"description": "the ucas statements that ran (error positions refer to them)", "type": "string"}, "structured": {"description": "result has fields beyond text", "type": "boolean"}, "result": {"description": "the command's fields (kind, ...); exact values as {value, exact}; expressions as ucas strings that parse back; unstructured commands give {text}", "type": "object"}, "results": {"description": "every result, when the request ran several commands", "type": "array"}, "notes": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"enum": ["rule", "info", "assumed", "default"]}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}}, "conditions": {"description": "where the answer holds", "type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}}, "checks": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"type": "string"}, "points": {"type": "integer"}, "max_diff": {"type": "number"}, "passed": {"type": "boolean"}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}}, "proof": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"enum": ["symbolic", "exhaustive", "sat", "numeric", "search"]}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}, "files": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"name": {"type": "string"}, "mime": {"type": "string"}, "bytes": {"type": "integer"}, "path": {"type": "string"}, "base64": {"type": "string"}}}}, "text": {"description": "the output as the CLI prints it", "type": "string"}, "error": {"type": "object", "required": ["code", "message"], "properties": {"code": {"enum": ["bad_json", "bad_request", "unknown_command", "parse_error", "domain_error", "unsupported", "failed", "ambiguous", "needs_input", "not_understood", "timeout", "internal"]}, "message": {"type": "string"}, "pos": {"type": "object", "properties": {"line": {"type": "integer"}, "col": {"type": "integer"}}}, "key": {"description": "ambiguous: the args.assume key that picks a reading", "type": "string"}, "readings": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"index": {"type": "integer"}, "reading": {"type": "string"}, "default": {"type": "boolean"}, "how": {"type": "string"}}}}, "how": {"type": "string"}}}}}}, {"name": "hypercomplex", "title": "Quaternions and octonions", "description": "Cayley-Dickson algebras (quaternion, octonion, sedenion, cd N): multiplication tables, algebra properties with counterexamples, zero divisors, associators, commutators, 3-D rotations by quaternions, axis-angle, rotation matrices, slerp.\n\nCall with {\"op\": OP, \"args\": {...}}; expressions are ucas syntax strings (x^2 sin(x), isqrt(x: u4)) or an AST ({\"op\": \"+\", \"args\": [...]}).  Ops (* = required arg):\n- multiplication_table(algebra*): an algebra's multiplication table (and the Fano plane)\n- algebra(algebra*, property): an algebra's properties with counterexamples\n- zerodivisors(algebra*): a pair of zero divisors\n- associator(a*, b*, c*): (ab)c - a(bc)\n- commutator(a*, b*): ab - ba\n- rotate(v*, by*, about): rotate a vector by a quaternion or an angle about an axis\n- axisangle(q*): axis and angle to a unit quaternion, or back\n- rotmatrix(q*): a quaternion's 3x3 rotation matrix\n- frommatrix(matrix*): the quaternion of a rotation matrix\n- slerp(q1*, q2*, t*): spherical linear interpolation\nEvery op also takes assume (answers to ambiguities, from an error's readings), defaults, timeout_s, files.  Example: {\"op\": \"multiplication_table\", \"args\": {\"f\": \"x^3 - 3x\"}}", "inputSchema": {"type": "object", "properties": {"op": {"type": "string", "enum": ["multiplication_table", "algebra", "zerodivisors", "associator", "commutator", "rotate", "axisangle", "rotmatrix", "frommatrix", "slerp"], "description": "the operation"}, "args": {"type": "object", "description": "the op's named arguments (see the description; the exact schema of each op is in the session tool's schema op)"}}, "required": ["op"], "additionalProperties": false}, "outputSchema": {"type": "object", "required": ["id", "ok", "cmd"], "properties": {"id": {"description": "the request's id, as given (null if none)"}, "ok": {"type": "boolean"}, "cmd": {"type": ["string", "null"]}, "ucas": {"description": "the ucas statements that ran (error positions refer to them)", "type": "string"}, "structured": {"description": "result has fields beyond text", "type": "boolean"}, "result": {"description": "the command's fields (kind, ...); exact values as {value, exact}; expressions as ucas strings that parse back; unstructured commands give {text}", "type": "object"}, "results": {"description": "every result, when the request ran several commands", "type": "array"}, "notes": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"enum": ["rule", "info", "assumed", "default"]}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}}, "conditions": {"description": "where the answer holds", "type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}}, "checks": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"type": "string"}, "points": {"type": "integer"}, "max_diff": {"type": "number"}, "passed": {"type": "boolean"}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}}, "proof": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"enum": ["symbolic", "exhaustive", "sat", "numeric", "search"]}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}, "files": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"name": {"type": "string"}, "mime": {"type": "string"}, "bytes": {"type": "integer"}, "path": {"type": "string"}, "base64": {"type": "string"}}}}, "text": {"description": "the output as the CLI prints it", "type": "string"}, "error": {"type": "object", "required": ["code", "message"], "properties": {"code": {"enum": ["bad_json", "bad_request", "unknown_command", "parse_error", "domain_error", "unsupported", "failed", "ambiguous", "needs_input", "not_understood", "timeout", "internal"]}, "message": {"type": "string"}, "pos": {"type": "object", "properties": {"line": {"type": "integer"}, "col": {"type": "integer"}}}, "key": {"description": "ambiguous: the args.assume key that picks a reading", "type": "string"}, "readings": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"index": {"type": "integer"}, "reading": {"type": "string"}, "default": {"type": "boolean"}, "how": {"type": "string"}}}}, "how": {"type": "string"}}}}}}, {"name": "rings", "title": "Rings and finite fields", "description": "Number theory and finite fields: Z/n, GF(p^n) (\"ring\": \"GF(2^8)\", \"modulus\": \"aes\"), Z[i]: inverses, orders, phi, factoring, Legendre/Jacobi, square roots mod n, primitive roots, discrete logs, CRT, congruences, division magic numbers, polynomials over GF(q) (factor, irreducible, primitive), matrices mod n, GF(2) bit maps.  A ring argument is \"ring\" and/or \"modulus\" (alone: mod N).\n\nCall with {\"op\": OP, \"args\": {...}}; expressions are ucas syntax strings (x^2 sin(x), isqrt(x: u4)) or an AST ({\"op\": \"+\", \"args\": [...]}).  Ops (* = required arg):\n- ring(ring, modulus, what): a ring's structure (units, zero divisors, ideals ...), an element of it, or a value computed in it\n- inverse_mod(a*, ring, modulus): a multiplicative inverse (of a number, an element, a matrix)\n- order_mod(a*, ring, modulus): multiplicative order (of a residue, an element, a polynomial over GF)\n- phi(n*): Euler's totient\n- carmichael(n*): Carmichael's lambda\n- factorint(n*): integer factorisation (Pollard-Brent, Miller-Rabin)\n- legendre(a*, p*): the Legendre symbol (a/p)\n- jacobi(a*, n*): the Jacobi symbol (a/n)\n- sqrtmod(a*, ring, modulus): square roots mod n (Tonelli-Shanks, Hensel, CRT)\n- qr(n*): the quadratic residues mod n\n- primroot(a, n, ring, modulus): the smallest primitive root mod n, or whether a is one\n- dlog(a*, base, ring, modulus): the discrete logarithm\n- crt(congruences*): the Chinese remainder theorem\n- congruence(equation*, ring, modulus): a linear or polynomial congruence\n- magic(divisor*, type*): the multiply-shift for dividing by a constant\n- ring_factor(p*, ring, modulus): factor a polynomial over a finite field or Z/n (or an element of Z[i])\n- irreducible(p*, ring, modulus): Rabin's irreducibility test\n- primitive(p*, ring, modulus): is the polynomial primitive\n- ring_roots(p*, ring, modulus): roots of a polynomial in Z/n or GF(q)\n- ring_poly(p*, ring, modulus): a polynomial expression reduced over a ring\n- ring_gcd(p*, q*, ring, modulus): polynomial (or Gaussian integer) gcd over a ring\n- ring_norm(a*, ring, modulus): the norm of a quadratic integer\n- matrix(matrix*, op, rhs, ring, modulus): a matrix over Z/n or GF(q): its properties, det, rank, nullspace, inverse, or a solve\n- gf2matrix(f*, type*): a GF(2)-linear bit map as a matrix\nEvery op also takes assume (answers to ambiguities, from an error's readings), defaults, timeout_s, files.  Example: {\"op\": \"ring\", \"args\": {\"f\": \"x^3 - 3x\"}}", "inputSchema": {"type": "object", "properties": {"op": {"type": "string", "enum": ["ring", "inverse_mod", "order_mod", "phi", "carmichael", "factorint", "legendre", "jacobi", "sqrtmod", "qr", "primroot", "dlog", "crt", "congruence", "magic", "ring_factor", "irreducible", "primitive", "ring_roots", "ring_poly", "ring_gcd", "ring_norm", "matrix", "gf2matrix"], "description": "the operation"}, "args": {"type": "object", "description": "the op's named arguments (see the description; the exact schema of each op is in the session tool's schema op)"}}, "required": ["op"], "additionalProperties": false}, "outputSchema": {"type": "object", "required": ["id", "ok", "cmd"], "properties": {"id": {"description": "the request's id, as given (null if none)"}, "ok": {"type": "boolean"}, "cmd": {"type": ["string", "null"]}, "ucas": {"description": "the ucas statements that ran (error positions refer to them)", "type": "string"}, "structured": {"description": "result has fields beyond text", "type": "boolean"}, "result": {"description": "the command's fields (kind, ...); exact values as {value, exact}; expressions as ucas strings that parse back; unstructured commands give {text}", "type": "object"}, "results": {"description": "every result, when the request ran several commands", "type": "array"}, "notes": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"enum": ["rule", "info", "assumed", "default"]}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}}, "conditions": {"description": "where the answer holds", "type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}}, "checks": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"type": "string"}, "points": {"type": "integer"}, "max_diff": {"type": "number"}, "passed": {"type": "boolean"}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}}, "proof": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"enum": ["symbolic", "exhaustive", "sat", "numeric", "search"]}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}, "files": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"name": {"type": "string"}, "mime": {"type": "string"}, "bytes": {"type": "integer"}, "path": {"type": "string"}, "base64": {"type": "string"}}}}, "text": {"description": "the output as the CLI prints it", "type": "string"}, "error": {"type": "object", "required": ["code", "message"], "properties": {"code": {"enum": ["bad_json", "bad_request", "unknown_command", "parse_error", "domain_error", "unsupported", "failed", "ambiguous", "needs_input", "not_understood", "timeout", "internal"]}, "message": {"type": "string"}, "pos": {"type": "object", "properties": {"line": {"type": "integer"}, "col": {"type": "integer"}}}, "key": {"description": "ambiguous: the args.assume key that picks a reading", "type": "string"}, "readings": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"index": {"type": "integer"}, "reading": {"type": "string"}, "default": {"type": "boolean"}, "how": {"type": "string"}}}}, "how": {"type": "string"}}}}}}, {"name": "transforms", "title": "Transforms and series", "description": "Laplace and Z transforms (with the region of convergence) and their inverses, ODEs and recurrences through them, transfer functions, Fourier transforms and series, DFT/DTFT, generating functions, infinite sums and products (test, closed form, numeric value), convergence, radius of convergence, power series, Euler-Maclaurin asymptotics.\n\nCall with {\"op\": OP, \"args\": {...}}; expressions are ucas syntax strings (x^2 sin(x), isqrt(x: u4)) or an AST ({\"op\": \"+\", \"args\": [...]}).  Ops (* = required arg):\n- laplace(f*, var, to_var, period): the one-sided Laplace transform, with its region of convergence\n- ilaplace(f*, var, to_var): the inverse Laplace transform\n- laplace_solve(equations*): a linear ODE with constant coefficients through the Laplace transform\n- ztrans(f*, var, to_var): the one-sided Z transform, with its ROC\n- iztrans(f*, var, to_var): the inverse Z transform (causal)\n- zsolve(equations*): a linear recurrence through the Z transform\n- tf(f*): a transfer function: poles, zeros, stability, impulse response\n- fourier(f*, var, to_var): the Fourier transform\n- ifourier(f*, var, to_var): the inverse Fourier transform\n- fourier_series(f*, var, on, period, terms): a Fourier series\n- dft(values*): the discrete Fourier transform (FFT for powers of two)\n- idft(values*): the inverse DFT\n- dtft(values, f): the discrete-time Fourier transform\n- genfunc(a*, var): the ordinary generating function\n- egf(a*): the exponential generating function\n- infinite_sum(index*, from, f*): an infinite sum: convergence test, closed form, numeric value\n- infinite_product(index*, from, f*): an infinite product\n- converge(a*): convergence tests of sum a_n\n- radius(a*): the radius and interval of convergence of a power series\n- powerseries(f*, var, at): the general term of a power series\n- asymptotic(sum*): Euler-Maclaurin asymptotics of a partial sum\nEvery op also takes assume (answers to ambiguities, from an error's readings), defaults, timeout_s, files.  Example: {\"op\": \"laplace\", \"args\": {\"f\": \"x^3 - 3x\"}}", "inputSchema": {"type": "object", "properties": {"op": {"type": "string", "enum": ["laplace", "ilaplace", "laplace_solve", "ztrans", "iztrans", "zsolve", "tf", "fourier", "ifourier", "fourier_series", "dft", "idft", "dtft", "genfunc", "egf", "infinite_sum", "infinite_product", "converge", "radius", "powerseries", "asymptotic"], "description": "the operation"}, "args": {"type": "object", "description": "the op's named arguments (see the description; the exact schema of each op is in the session tool's schema op)"}}, "required": ["op"], "additionalProperties": false}, "outputSchema": {"type": "object", "required": ["id", "ok", "cmd"], "properties": {"id": {"description": "the request's id, as given (null if none)"}, "ok": {"type": "boolean"}, "cmd": {"type": ["string", "null"]}, "ucas": {"description": "the ucas statements that ran (error positions refer to them)", "type": "string"}, "structured": {"description": "result has fields beyond text", "type": "boolean"}, "result": {"description": "the command's fields (kind, ...); exact values as {value, exact}; expressions as ucas strings that parse back; unstructured commands give {text}", "type": "object"}, "results": {"description": "every result, when the request ran several commands", "type": "array"}, "notes": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"enum": ["rule", "info", "assumed", "default"]}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}}, "conditions": {"description": "where the answer holds", "type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}}, "checks": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"type": "string"}, "points": {"type": "integer"}, "max_diff": {"type": "number"}, "passed": {"type": "boolean"}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}}, "proof": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"enum": ["symbolic", "exhaustive", "sat", "numeric", "search"]}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}, "files": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"name": {"type": "string"}, "mime": {"type": "string"}, "bytes": {"type": "integer"}, "path": {"type": "string"}, "base64": {"type": "string"}}}}, "text": {"description": "the output as the CLI prints it", "type": "string"}, "error": {"type": "object", "required": ["code", "message"], "properties": {"code": {"enum": ["bad_json", "bad_request", "unknown_command", "parse_error", "domain_error", "unsupported", "failed", "ambiguous", "needs_input", "not_understood", "timeout", "internal"]}, "message": {"type": "string"}, "pos": {"type": "object", "properties": {"line": {"type": "integer"}, "col": {"type": "integer"}}}, "key": {"description": "ambiguous: the args.assume key that picks a reading", "type": "string"}, "readings": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"index": {"type": "integer"}, "reading": {"type": "string"}, "default": {"type": "boolean"}, "how": {"type": "string"}}}}, "how": {"type": "string"}}}}}}, {"name": "solids", "title": "Areas and solids of revolution", "description": "Areas under and between curves, solids of revolution (volume by disks/washers/shells, surface area, Pappus), arc length, centroids: exact and numeric values, checks, and a picture.\n\nCall with {\"op\": OP, \"args\": {...}}; expressions are ucas syntax strings (x^2 sin(x), isqrt(x: u4)) or an AST ({\"op\": \"+\", \"args\": [...]}).  Ops (* = required arg):\n- area(f*, from, to, options, nofile): the area under or between curves (exact and numeric; a GIF)\n- revolve(f*, from, to, about, method, options, nofile): the solid of revolution: volume, surface, centroid, Pappus (a GIF)\n- volume(f*, from, to, about, method, nofile): the volume of the solid of revolution\n- surfacearea(f*, from, to, about, nofile): the lateral surface area of the solid\n- arclength(f*, from, to, nofile): the arc length of a curve\n- centroid(f*, from, to, nofile): the centroid of the region under or between curves\nEvery op also takes assume (answers to ambiguities, from an error's readings), defaults, timeout_s, files.  Example: {\"op\": \"area\", \"args\": {\"f\": \"x^3 - 3x\"}}", "inputSchema": {"type": "object", "properties": {"op": {"type": "string", "enum": ["area", "revolve", "volume", "surfacearea", "arclength", "centroid"], "description": "the operation"}, "args": {"type": "object", "description": "the op's named arguments (see the description; the exact schema of each op is in the session tool's schema op)"}}, "required": ["op"], "additionalProperties": false}, "outputSchema": {"type": "object", "required": ["id", "ok", "cmd"], "properties": {"id": {"description": "the request's id, as given (null if none)"}, "ok": {"type": "boolean"}, "cmd": {"type": ["string", "null"]}, "ucas": {"description": "the ucas statements that ran (error positions refer to them)", "type": "string"}, "structured": {"description": "result has fields beyond text", "type": "boolean"}, "result": {"description": "the command's fields (kind, ...); exact values as {value, exact}; expressions as ucas strings that parse back; unstructured commands give {text}", "type": "object"}, "results": {"description": "every result, when the request ran several commands", "type": "array"}, "notes": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"enum": ["rule", "info", "assumed", "default"]}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}}, "conditions": {"description": "where the answer holds", "type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}}, "checks": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"type": "string"}, "points": {"type": "integer"}, "max_diff": {"type": "number"}, "passed": {"type": "boolean"}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}}, "proof": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"enum": ["symbolic", "exhaustive", "sat", "numeric", "search"]}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}, "files": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"name": {"type": "string"}, "mime": {"type": "string"}, "bytes": {"type": "integer"}, "path": {"type": "string"}, "base64": {"type": "string"}}}}, "text": {"description": "the output as the CLI prints it", "type": "string"}, "error": {"type": "object", "required": ["code", "message"], "properties": {"code": {"enum": ["bad_json", "bad_request", "unknown_command", "parse_error", "domain_error", "unsupported", "failed", "ambiguous", "needs_input", "not_understood", "timeout", "internal"]}, "message": {"type": "string"}, "pos": {"type": "object", "properties": {"line": {"type": "integer"}, "col": {"type": "integer"}}}, "key": {"description": "ambiguous: the args.assume key that picks a reading", "type": "string"}, "readings": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"index": {"type": "integer"}, "reading": {"type": "string"}, "default": {"type": "boolean"}, "how": {"type": "string"}}}}, "how": {"type": "string"}}}}}}, {"name": "plot", "title": "Plots and animations", "description": "GIF plots of functions, curves, regions, surfaces, vector and slope fields (bounds chosen from the function's features), and animations of scans and SIMD execution.  The GIF comes back as an image.\n\nCall with {\"op\": OP, \"args\": {...}}; expressions are ucas syntax strings (x^2 sin(x), isqrt(x: u4)) or an AST ({\"op\": \"+\", \"args\": [...]}).  Ops (* = required arg):\n- plot(fs*, options, to, nofile): a GIF plot (files)\n- plot3d(f*, options, to, nofile): a surface (files)\n- neighbourhood(f*, at, nofile): a plot around the interesting part (files)\n- animate(spec, code, inputs, output_format, size, sampler, seed, lanes, to, nofile): an animated GIF: scans, lockstep execution, a shader over images (files)\nEvery op also takes assume (answers to ambiguities, from an error's readings), defaults, timeout_s, files.  Example: {\"op\": \"plot\", \"args\": {\"f\": \"x^3 - 3x\"}}", "inputSchema": {"type": "object", "properties": {"op": {"type": "string", "enum": ["plot", "plot3d", "neighbourhood", "animate"], "description": "the operation"}, "args": {"type": "object", "description": "the op's named arguments (see the description; the exact schema of each op is in the session tool's schema op)"}}, "required": ["op"], "additionalProperties": false}, "outputSchema": {"type": "object", "required": ["id", "ok", "cmd"], "properties": {"id": {"description": "the request's id, as given (null if none)"}, "ok": {"type": "boolean"}, "cmd": {"type": ["string", "null"]}, "ucas": {"description": "the ucas statements that ran (error positions refer to them)", "type": "string"}, "structured": {"description": "result has fields beyond text", "type": "boolean"}, "result": {"description": "the command's fields (kind, ...); exact values as {value, exact}; expressions as ucas strings that parse back; unstructured commands give {text}", "type": "object"}, "results": {"description": "every result, when the request ran several commands", "type": "array"}, "notes": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"enum": ["rule", "info", "assumed", "default"]}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}}, "conditions": {"description": "where the answer holds", "type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}}, "checks": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"type": "string"}, "points": {"type": "integer"}, "max_diff": {"type": "number"}, "passed": {"type": "boolean"}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}}, "proof": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"enum": ["symbolic", "exhaustive", "sat", "numeric", "search"]}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}, "files": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"name": {"type": "string"}, "mime": {"type": "string"}, "bytes": {"type": "integer"}, "path": {"type": "string"}, "base64": {"type": "string"}}}}, "text": {"description": "the output as the CLI prints it", "type": "string"}, "error": {"type": "object", "required": ["code", "message"], "properties": {"code": {"enum": ["bad_json", "bad_request", "unknown_command", "parse_error", "domain_error", "unsupported", "failed", "ambiguous", "needs_input", "not_understood", "timeout", "internal"]}, "message": {"type": "string"}, "pos": {"type": "object", "properties": {"line": {"type": "integer"}, "col": {"type": "integer"}}}, "key": {"description": "ambiguous: the args.assume key that picks a reading", "type": "string"}, "readings": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"index": {"type": "integer"}, "reading": {"type": "string"}, "default": {"type": "boolean"}, "how": {"type": "string"}}}}, "how": {"type": "string"}}}}}}, {"name": "c", "title": "C optimiser", "description": "C99 in, faster C out for a chosen x86-64 target (zen4, skylake, alderlake, x86-64-v2/v3/v4 ...): each function or expression is lowered with C99 LP64 semantics (promotions, wrap, UB as a domain condition, IEEE float and double) and rewritten only by forms proved equal on every input (exhaustively, by SAT, by a stated derivation, or by induction for loops summed in closed form); loops over arrays are rewritten per element, strlen-style scans become strlen; c_lower shows each loop's IR for the vectoriser; optional differential test and rdtsc benchmark with the host cc.\n\nCall with {\"op\": OP, \"args\": {...}}; expressions are ucas syntax strings (x^2 sin(x), isqrt(x: u4)) or an AST ({\"op\": \"+\", \"args\": [...]}).  Ops (* = required arg):\n- c_optimize(code, file, target, budget, range, check, bench, wrapv, nofile, timed, trace, vecstub, vectorize, engines, steps, ebudget, approx, error): C99 in, faster C out for an x86-64 target: each rewrite proved (exhaustively, by SAT, by a derivation or by induction) against the original under C99 LP64 semantics with IEEE floats, unproved ones not applied; loops in closed form, element-wise loop bodies, strlen scans, loops vectorised with intrinsics (proved lane by lane)\n- c_lower(code, file, wrapv): each C function as one ucas value of its parameters (with the C UB as a domain condition), or why not; for the others, each counted loop in the vectoriser's IR\n- c_targets(): the x86-64 targets and their instruction-set features\nEvery op also takes assume (answers to ambiguities, from an error's readings), defaults, timeout_s, files.  Example: {\"op\": \"c_optimize\", \"args\": {\"f\": \"x^3 - 3x\"}}", "inputSchema": {"type": "object", "properties": {"op": {"type": "string", "enum": ["c_optimize", "c_lower", "c_targets"], "description": "the operation"}, "args": {"type": "object", "description": "the op's named arguments (see the description; the exact schema of each op is in the session tool's schema op)"}}, "required": ["op"], "additionalProperties": false}, "outputSchema": {"type": "object", "required": ["id", "ok", "cmd"], "properties": {"id": {"description": "the request's id, as given (null if none)"}, "ok": {"type": "boolean"}, "cmd": {"type": ["string", "null"]}, "ucas": {"description": "the ucas statements that ran (error positions refer to them)", "type": "string"}, "structured": {"description": "result has fields beyond text", "type": "boolean"}, "result": {"description": "the command's fields (kind, ...); exact values as {value, exact}; expressions as ucas strings that parse back; unstructured commands give {text}", "type": "object"}, "results": {"description": "every result, when the request ran several commands", "type": "array"}, "notes": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"enum": ["rule", "info", "assumed", "default"]}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}}, "conditions": {"description": "where the answer holds", "type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}}, "checks": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"type": "string"}, "points": {"type": "integer"}, "max_diff": {"type": "number"}, "passed": {"type": "boolean"}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}}, "proof": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"enum": ["symbolic", "exhaustive", "sat", "numeric", "search"]}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}, "files": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"name": {"type": "string"}, "mime": {"type": "string"}, "bytes": {"type": "integer"}, "path": {"type": "string"}, "base64": {"type": "string"}}}}, "text": {"description": "the output as the CLI prints it", "type": "string"}, "error": {"type": "object", "required": ["code", "message"], "properties": {"code": {"enum": ["bad_json", "bad_request", "unknown_command", "parse_error", "domain_error", "unsupported", "failed", "ambiguous", "needs_input", "not_understood", "timeout", "internal"]}, "message": {"type": "string"}, "pos": {"type": "object", "properties": {"line": {"type": "integer"}, "col": {"type": "integer"}}}, "key": {"description": "ambiguous: the args.assume key that picks a reading", "type": "string"}, "readings": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"index": {"type": "integer"}, "reading": {"type": "string"}, "default": {"type": "boolean"}, "how": {"type": "string"}}}}, "how": {"type": "string"}}}}}}, {"name": "x86", "title": "x86-64 costs and intrinsics", "description": "x86-64 cost models per µarch (Skylake, Skylake-X, Golden Cove, Raptor Lake, Zen 4, x86-64-v2/v3/v4; numbers typed from uops.info, Agner Fog and the vendor manuals, a few measured on this host, the rest estimates, each row tagged), a cycle-level throughput estimate of a function's x86 code (mca), and the intrinsics catalogue (SSE2 .. AVX-512, BMI, GFNI, AES, CLMUL) with exact lane semantics as ucas expressions, tested against the C compiler (x86check).\n\nCall with {\"op\": OP, \"args\": {...}}; expressions are ucas syntax strings (x^2 sin(x), isqrt(x: u4)) or an AST ({\"op\": \"+\", \"args\": [...]}).  Ops (* = required arg):\n- x86_models(): the x86 µarch cost models (skl skx glc rpl zen4 x86v2 x86v3 x86v4)\n- x86_model(name*): one x86 µarch: features, ports, and per instruction class latency, reciprocal throughput, uops and ports at xmm/ymm/zmm (with where each number comes from)\n- mca(f*, model): a cycle-level throughput estimate of a function's x86 code (critical path, port pressure, front end; no caches or mispredictions)\n- intrinsic(name*, model): one x86 intrinsic: signature, features, instruction class, exact lane semantics (as ucas expressions) and costs per µarch\n- intrinsics(filter, model): the intrinsics catalogue: count per feature, or the names matching a filter (a substring, a feature such as avx2, or a class)\n- x86check(filter, n, avx512): test the intrinsics' lane semantics against the host C compiler's intrinsics (compiled and run on random and edge inputs)\nEvery op also takes assume (answers to ambiguities, from an error's readings), defaults, timeout_s, files.  Example: {\"op\": \"x86_models\", \"args\": {\"f\": \"x^3 - 3x\"}}", "inputSchema": {"type": "object", "properties": {"op": {"type": "string", "enum": ["x86_models", "x86_model", "mca", "intrinsic", "intrinsics", "x86check"], "description": "the operation"}, "args": {"type": "object", "description": "the op's named arguments (see the description; the exact schema of each op is in the session tool's schema op)"}}, "required": ["op"], "additionalProperties": false}, "outputSchema": {"type": "object", "required": ["id", "ok", "cmd"], "properties": {"id": {"description": "the request's id, as given (null if none)"}, "ok": {"type": "boolean"}, "cmd": {"type": ["string", "null"]}, "ucas": {"description": "the ucas statements that ran (error positions refer to them)", "type": "string"}, "structured": {"description": "result has fields beyond text", "type": "boolean"}, "result": {"description": "the command's fields (kind, ...); exact values as {value, exact}; expressions as ucas strings that parse back; unstructured commands give {text}", "type": "object"}, "results": {"description": "every result, when the request ran several commands", "type": "array"}, "notes": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"enum": ["rule", "info", "assumed", "default"]}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}}, "conditions": {"description": "where the answer holds", "type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}}, "checks": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"type": "string"}, "points": {"type": "integer"}, "max_diff": {"type": "number"}, "passed": {"type": "boolean"}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}}, "proof": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"enum": ["symbolic", "exhaustive", "sat", "numeric", "search"]}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}, "files": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"name": {"type": "string"}, "mime": {"type": "string"}, "bytes": {"type": "integer"}, "path": {"type": "string"}, "base64": {"type": "string"}}}}, "text": {"description": "the output as the CLI prints it", "type": "string"}, "error": {"type": "object", "required": ["code", "message"], "properties": {"code": {"enum": ["bad_json", "bad_request", "unknown_command", "parse_error", "domain_error", "unsupported", "failed", "ambiguous", "needs_input", "not_understood", "timeout", "internal"]}, "message": {"type": "string"}, "pos": {"type": "object", "properties": {"line": {"type": "integer"}, "col": {"type": "integer"}}}, "key": {"description": "ambiguous: the args.assume key that picks a reading", "type": "string"}, "readings": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"index": {"type": "integer"}, "reading": {"type": "string"}, "default": {"type": "boolean"}, "how": {"type": "string"}}}}, "how": {"type": "string"}}}}}}, {"name": "abstract_algebra", "title": "Abstract algebra, exactly", "description": "Exact algebra with certificates: integers of any size (bigint), integer matrices (Smith and Hermite forms with unimodular transforms, kernels, images, solving over Z; rational matrices), finitely generated abelian groups (\"Z/4 + Z/6\", \"coker [[2, 0], [0, 3]]\"): invariants, isomorphisms with explicit maps, Hom, tensor, Tor, Ext, homomorphisms with kernel/image/cokernel, subgroups, element orders, exactness; permutation groups by Schreier-Sims (\"S4\", \"(1 2 3), (1 2)\": order, orbits, solvable, nilpotent, centre, membership, subgroups, cosets, homomorphisms) and Cayley tables; polynomial ideals over Q and F_p (Groebner bases with cofactors, membership certificates, ideal equality); modules over F[x] (Smith form, rational canonical form).  Every claim is checked (U A V = D, preimages, inverse maps) and the check is reported.  For instance {\"op\": \"abiso\", \"args\": {\"g\": \"Z/4 + Z/6\", \"h\": \"Z/2 + Z/12\"}} or {\"op\": \"snf\", \"args\": {\"matrix\": [[2, 4], [6, 8]]}}.\n\nCall with {\"op\": OP, \"args\": {...}}; expressions are ucas syntax strings (x^2 sin(x), isqrt(x: u4)) or an AST ({\"op\": \"+\", \"args\": [...]}).  Ops (* = required arg):\n- bigint(expr*): an exact integer expression of any size (+ - * ^ !, / exact, div floor, % mod, gcd, lcm, abs, isprime, binomial)\n- bigint_factor(n*): prime factorization of an integer of any size (Pollard-Brent rho; product and primality checked)\n- snf(matrix*): Smith normal form U A V = D with U, V and their inverses, verified; the cokernel\n- hnf(matrix*): row Hermite normal form H = U A with U unimodular, verified\n- zmatrix(op, matrix*, rhs): an integer matrix over Z: summary, det, rank, kernel (saturated basis), image (lattice basis), inverse over Z, cokernel group, or solve A x = b over Z\n- qmatrix(op, matrix*, rhs): a matrix over Q (entries like \"1/2\"): rref, det, rank, inverse, nullspace, solve\n- abgroup(group*): a finitely generated abelian group: invariant factors, primary decomposition, order, rank, exponent, torsion, generators\n- abiso(g*, h*): are two abelian groups isomorphic; if so an explicit isomorphism and its inverse, both checked\n- abhom(g*, h*): the group Hom(G, H)\n- abtensor(g*, h*): the tensor product G (x) H\n- abtor(g*, h*): Tor(G, H) from a free resolution\n- abext(g*, h*): Ext(G, H) from a free resolution\n- abmap(from*, to*, matrix*): a homomorphism G -> H given by the images of G's generators (columns, in H's generators): well defined?, kernel, image, cokernel, injective, surjective, inverse\n- abelem(group*, element*): an element of an abelian group: canonical form and order\n- absub(group*, generators*): the subgroup generated by elements, its quotient and index (membership witnesses checked)\n- abexact(g1*, g2*, g3*, f*, g*): is G1 -f-> G2 -g-> G3 exact at G2 (with preimages of ker g as the certificate)\n- permgroup(group*): a permutation group by Schreier-Sims: order (exact, any size), base and strong generators, orbits, abelian, derived and lower central series, solvable, nilpotent, centre\n- permelem(group*, perm*): is a permutation in the group (sifting, with the word in the transversals as the certificate); its order\n- permsub(h*, g*): H in G: subgroup?, normal?, index, normal closure, coset representatives\n- permhom(from*, to*, images*): does sending G's generators to the given permutations define a homomorphism G -> H\n- cayley(table*): a finite group by its Cayley table (entries 0..n-1): the axioms checked, abelian, element orders, solvable, nilpotent\n- groebner(polys*, order, modulus, vars): the reduced Groebner basis of an ideal of polynomials over Q or F_p, each element with its cofactors in the generators (Buchberger with criteria; verified)\n- idealmember(h*, polys*, order, modulus, vars): is h in the ideal: the cofactors h = sum c_j f_j (multiplied out and checked), or the nonzero normal form\n- idealeq(i*, j*, order, modulus, vars): compare two ideals: equal, one inside the other, or neither (each inclusion certified by cofactors)\n- fxmodule(matrix*, modulus): F^n as an F[x]-module with x acting by a matrix: invariant factors, minimal and characteristic polynomial, rational canonical form (Smith form over F[x])\n- pmsnf(matrix*, modulus): the Smith normal form of a matrix of polynomials in one variable over Q or F_p, with U and V\nEvery op also takes assume (answers to ambiguities, from an error's readings), defaults, timeout_s, files.  Example: {\"op\": \"bigint\", \"args\": {\"f\": \"x^3 - 3x\"}}", "inputSchema": {"type": "object", "properties": {"op": {"type": "string", "enum": ["bigint", "bigint_factor", "snf", "hnf", "zmatrix", "qmatrix", "abgroup", "abiso", "abhom", "abtensor", "abtor", "abext", "abmap", "abelem", "absub", "abexact", "permgroup", "permelem", "permsub", "permhom", "cayley", "groebner", "idealmember", "idealeq", "fxmodule", "pmsnf"], "description": "the operation"}, "args": {"type": "object", "description": "the op's named arguments (see the description; the exact schema of each op is in the session tool's schema op)"}}, "required": ["op"], "additionalProperties": false}, "outputSchema": {"type": "object", "required": ["id", "ok", "cmd"], "properties": {"id": {"description": "the request's id, as given (null if none)"}, "ok": {"type": "boolean"}, "cmd": {"type": ["string", "null"]}, "ucas": {"description": "the ucas statements that ran (error positions refer to them)", "type": "string"}, "structured": {"description": "result has fields beyond text", "type": "boolean"}, "result": {"description": "the command's fields (kind, ...); exact values as {value, exact}; expressions as ucas strings that parse back; unstructured commands give {text}", "type": "object"}, "results": {"description": "every result, when the request ran several commands", "type": "array"}, "notes": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"enum": ["rule", "info", "assumed", "default"]}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}}, "conditions": {"description": "where the answer holds", "type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}}, "checks": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"type": "string"}, "points": {"type": "integer"}, "max_diff": {"type": "number"}, "passed": {"type": "boolean"}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}}, "proof": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"enum": ["symbolic", "exhaustive", "sat", "numeric", "search"]}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}, "files": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"name": {"type": "string"}, "mime": {"type": "string"}, "bytes": {"type": "integer"}, "path": {"type": "string"}, "base64": {"type": "string"}}}}, "text": {"description": "the output as the CLI prints it", "type": "string"}, "error": {"type": "object", "required": ["code", "message"], "properties": {"code": {"enum": ["bad_json", "bad_request", "unknown_command", "parse_error", "domain_error", "unsupported", "failed", "ambiguous", "needs_input", "not_understood", "timeout", "internal"]}, "message": {"type": "string"}, "pos": {"type": "object", "properties": {"line": {"type": "integer"}, "col": {"type": "integer"}}}, "key": {"description": "ambiguous: the args.assume key that picks a reading", "type": "string"}, "readings": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"index": {"type": "integer"}, "reading": {"type": "string"}, "default": {"type": "boolean"}, "how": {"type": "string"}}}}, "how": {"type": "string"}}}}}}, {"name": "elliptic", "title": "Elliptic curves and Diophantine equations", "description": "Elliptic curves over Q, exactly (analytic values with error bounds): invariants, minimal models, Tate's algorithm, conductor, torsion, rank by 2-isogeny descent, generators, canonical heights, the group law, models (Montgomery, Edwards, Legendre) with their maps, periods, L-values, BSD; Diophantine equations reduced to elliptic curves (\"a/(b+c) + b/(a+c) + c/(a+b) = 4\" positive), congruent numbers, Mordell curves, sums of two cubes.  A curve is \"[a1, a2, a3, a4, a6]\", \"[a4, a6]\" or \"y^2 = x^3 - x\".  For instance {\"op\": \"diophantine\", \"args\": {\"equation\": \"a/(b+c) + b/(a+c) + c/(a+b) = 4\", \"positive\": true}}.\n\nCall with {\"op\": OP, \"args\": {...}}; expressions are ucas syntax strings (x^2 sin(x), isqrt(x: u4)) or an AST ({\"op\": \"+\", \"args\": [...]}).  Ops (* = required arg):\n- elliptic(curve*, op, args): an elliptic curve over Q: by default the summary (invariants, minimal model, Tate's algorithm: Kodaira symbols, c_p, conductor; torsion; rank bounds by 2-isogeny descent; generators and heights; periods, root number, L-values, analytic rank, BSD quotient), or one operation\n- diophantine(equation*, positive, integer, nonzero, count, maxmult, search): solve a Diophantine equation through an elliptic curve: a plane cubic (homogeneous in 3 variables, or affine in 2), a curve quadratic in one variable with a quartic discriminant, or z^2 = quartic(x, y); rational point, birational map to Weierstrass form (kept with its inverse), the group, combinations of generators mapped back, each solution substituted into the equation; with no solution, a proof where one is found (rank 0, or no rational point on the real component the conditions need)\n- weierstrass(equation*): the maps from a cubic or quartic curve to Weierstrass form, the minimal model and the group\n- congruent(n*): is n the area of a right triangle with rational sides: the curve y^2 = x^3 - n^2 x, its rank by descent, a triangle (checked) or a proof that none exists, Tunnell's counts\n- mordell(k*, bound): the Mordell curve y^2 = x^3 + k: the summary and its integral points up to a bound\n- cubesum(k*, positive): k as a sum of two rational cubes: x^3 + y^3 = k z^3 solved through its curve\nEvery op also takes assume (answers to ambiguities, from an error's readings), defaults, timeout_s, files.  Example: {\"op\": \"elliptic\", \"args\": {\"f\": \"x^3 - 3x\"}}", "inputSchema": {"type": "object", "properties": {"op": {"type": "string", "enum": ["elliptic", "diophantine", "weierstrass", "congruent", "mordell", "cubesum"], "description": "the operation"}, "args": {"type": "object", "description": "the op's named arguments (see the description; the exact schema of each op is in the session tool's schema op)"}}, "required": ["op"], "additionalProperties": false}, "outputSchema": {"type": "object", "required": ["id", "ok", "cmd"], "properties": {"id": {"description": "the request's id, as given (null if none)"}, "ok": {"type": "boolean"}, "cmd": {"type": ["string", "null"]}, "ucas": {"description": "the ucas statements that ran (error positions refer to them)", "type": "string"}, "structured": {"description": "result has fields beyond text", "type": "boolean"}, "result": {"description": "the command's fields (kind, ...); exact values as {value, exact}; expressions as ucas strings that parse back; unstructured commands give {text}", "type": "object"}, "results": {"description": "every result, when the request ran several commands", "type": "array"}, "notes": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"enum": ["rule", "info", "assumed", "default"]}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}}, "conditions": {"description": "where the answer holds", "type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}}, "checks": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"type": "string"}, "points": {"type": "integer"}, "max_diff": {"type": "number"}, "passed": {"type": "boolean"}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}}, "proof": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"enum": ["symbolic", "exhaustive", "sat", "numeric", "search"]}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}, "files": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"name": {"type": "string"}, "mime": {"type": "string"}, "bytes": {"type": "integer"}, "path": {"type": "string"}, "base64": {"type": "string"}}}}, "text": {"description": "the output as the CLI prints it", "type": "string"}, "error": {"type": "object", "required": ["code", "message"], "properties": {"code": {"enum": ["bad_json", "bad_request", "unknown_command", "parse_error", "domain_error", "unsupported", "failed", "ambiguous", "needs_input", "not_understood", "timeout", "internal"]}, "message": {"type": "string"}, "pos": {"type": "object", "properties": {"line": {"type": "integer"}, "col": {"type": "integer"}}}, "key": {"description": "ambiguous: the args.assume key that picks a reading", "type": "string"}, "readings": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"index": {"type": "integer"}, "reading": {"type": "string"}, "default": {"type": "boolean"}, "how": {"type": "string"}}}}, "how": {"type": "string"}}}}}}, {"name": "elliptic_ff", "title": "Elliptic curves over finite fields and cryptography", "description": "Curves over F_p (any size to 521 bits; named: secp256k1, P-256, P-384, P-521, Curve25519, Ed25519, Curve448, BN254, BLS12-381) and GF(2^m): #E by naive/BSGS/CM/Schoof with a certificate, group structure, twists, embedding degrees, scalar multiplication, ECDSA (RFC 6979), ECDH, X25519/X448, Ed25519, SEC 1 encodings, test vectors; discrete logs (Pohlig-Hellman, rho, MOV, Smart); Weil/Tate pairings; CM and Hilbert class polynomials; modular polynomials, Velu isogenies, isogeny graphs, division polynomials; ECM factoring and ECPP certificates.  A curve is a name, \"y^2 = x^3 + 2x + 3 mod 97\" or \"[a, b] mod p\".  Mathematics, not hardened (constant-time) cryptography.\n\nCall with {\"op\": OP, \"args\": {...}}; expressions are ucas syntax strings (x^2 sin(x), isqrt(x: u4)) or an AST ({\"op\": \"+\", \"args\": [...]}).  Ops (* = required arg):\n- ec_info(curve*): a curve over F_p: discriminant, j, #E (certified by point orders), trace, group structure (certified by a Weil pairing), twist, embedding degree, weaknesses\n- ec_order(curve*, method, timed): #E(F_p) by a chosen method, with the certificate (points whose orders leave one candidate in the Hasse interval)\n- ec_points(curve*): the points of E(F_p), p <= 100000\n- ec_add(curve*, P*, Q*): P + Q\n- ec_mul(curve*, k*, P*, method): k P by wNAF/Jacobian, checked against affine double-and-add, the Montgomery ladder and plain NAF\n- ecm(n*, B1, B2): factor an integer (up to 576 bits): trial division, Pollard rho, Lenstra ECM stage 1 + 2; with B1 one ECM run\n- ecdsa_sign(curve*, key*, hash, nonce, msg*): ECDSA signature with RFC 6979 deterministic nonce (variable-time code: mathematics, not a hardened implementation)\n- ecdsa_verify(curve*, pub*, r*, s*, hash, msg*): verify an ECDSA signature\n- ecdh(curve*, a*, b, pub): Diffie-Hellman on a named curve: both sides from two private keys, or one key and a peer's point (validated)\n- x25519(k*, u): RFC 7748 X25519 (hex, little-endian)\n- x448(k*, u): RFC 7748 X448 (hex, little-endian)\n- ed25519_sign(secret*, msghex*): RFC 8032 Ed25519 signature (and the public key)\n- ed25519_verify(pub*, sig*, msghex*): verify an Ed25519 signature\n- ec_compress(curve*, P*): SEC 1 encodings of a point\n- ec_decompress(curve*, hex*): decode a SEC 1 point\n- ec_validate(curve*, P*): public-key validation (SEC 1 3.2.2.1)\n- ec_vectors(): run the built-in RFC/FIPS test vectors and the named curves' parameter checks\n- ec_dlog(curve*, P*, Q, secret, method): a discrete logarithm k with k P = Q: Pohlig-Hellman, BSGS, rho, MOV (pairing transfer), Smart (anomalous); checked by k P = Q\n- ec_weak(kind*, bits*): generate a weak curve (anomalous: #E = p; supersingular: embedding degree 2); \"anomalous 64\" also works as the curve of ec_dlog\n- ec_pairing(curve*, P, Q, n, kind): Weil or reduced Tate pairing by Miller's algorithm with bilinearity checks; on bn254/bls12_381 alone: e(G1, G2) in F_p^12\n- hilbert(D*): the Hilbert class polynomial H_D (CM j-invariants), rounding error bounded\n- ec_cm(D*, p, bits): a CM curve with discriminant D over F_p, or a random prime-order CM curve of a given size\n- ecpp(n*): an Atkin-Morain ECPP primality certificate, verified by an independent checker\n- modpoly(l*, p): the classical modular polynomial Phi_l (over Z, or mod p)\n- ec_isogeny(curve*, kernel, l): an isogeny from a kernel point (Velu, Kohel, checked as a homomorphism), or the rational l-isogenies (roots of Phi_l)\n- ec_volcano(curve*, l*): the l-isogeny graph around j(E)\n- ec_divpoly(curve*, n*): the division polynomial psi_n, its roots and factor degrees (the torsion field)\n- ec_binary(curve*, mul): a binary curve y^2 + xy = x^3 + a x^2 + b over GF(2^m): count (Koblitz, naive), FIPS parameters checked\nEvery op also takes assume (answers to ambiguities, from an error's readings), defaults, timeout_s, files.  Example: {\"op\": \"ec_info\", \"args\": {\"f\": \"x^3 - 3x\"}}", "inputSchema": {"type": "object", "properties": {"op": {"type": "string", "enum": ["ec_info", "ec_order", "ec_points", "ec_add", "ec_mul", "ecm", "ecdsa_sign", "ecdsa_verify", "ecdh", "x25519", "x448", "ed25519_sign", "ed25519_verify", "ec_compress", "ec_decompress", "ec_validate", "ec_vectors", "ec_dlog", "ec_weak", "ec_pairing", "hilbert", "ec_cm", "ecpp", "modpoly", "ec_isogeny", "ec_volcano", "ec_divpoly", "ec_binary"], "description": "the operation"}, "args": {"type": "object", "description": "the op's named arguments (see the description; the exact schema of each op is in the session tool's schema op)"}}, "required": ["op"], "additionalProperties": false}, "outputSchema": {"type": "object", "required": ["id", "ok", "cmd"], "properties": {"id": {"description": "the request's id, as given (null if none)"}, "ok": {"type": "boolean"}, "cmd": {"type": ["string", "null"]}, "ucas": {"description": "the ucas statements that ran (error positions refer to them)", "type": "string"}, "structured": {"description": "result has fields beyond text", "type": "boolean"}, "result": {"description": "the command's fields (kind, ...); exact values as {value, exact}; expressions as ucas strings that parse back; unstructured commands give {text}", "type": "object"}, "results": {"description": "every result, when the request ran several commands", "type": "array"}, "notes": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"enum": ["rule", "info", "assumed", "default"]}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}}, "conditions": {"description": "where the answer holds", "type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}}, "checks": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"type": "string"}, "points": {"type": "integer"}, "max_diff": {"type": "number"}, "passed": {"type": "boolean"}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}}, "proof": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"enum": ["symbolic", "exhaustive", "sat", "numeric", "search"]}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}, "files": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"name": {"type": "string"}, "mime": {"type": "string"}, "bytes": {"type": "integer"}, "path": {"type": "string"}, "base64": {"type": "string"}}}}, "text": {"description": "the output as the CLI prints it", "type": "string"}, "error": {"type": "object", "required": ["code", "message"], "properties": {"code": {"enum": ["bad_json", "bad_request", "unknown_command", "parse_error", "domain_error", "unsupported", "failed", "ambiguous", "needs_input", "not_understood", "timeout", "internal"]}, "message": {"type": "string"}, "pos": {"type": "object", "properties": {"line": {"type": "integer"}, "col": {"type": "integer"}}}, "key": {"description": "ambiguous: the args.assume key that picks a reading", "type": "string"}, "readings": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"index": {"type": "integer"}, "reading": {"type": "string"}, "default": {"type": "boolean"}, "how": {"type": "string"}}}}, "how": {"type": "string"}}}}}}, {"name": "session", "title": "Session", "description": "The session: define a function (typed parameters), list the state, keep answers to ambiguities (assume), reset, the interface schema, the cost models.\n\nCall with {\"op\": OP, \"args\": {...}}; expressions are ucas syntax strings (x^2 sin(x), isqrt(x: u4)) or an AST ({\"op\": \"+\", \"args\": [...]}).  Ops (* = required arg):\n- define(name*, params, body*, where): define a function: name(params) = body [where ...]; every parameter needs a type (or a range)\n- state(): the session: functions, models, bases, assumptions\n- assume(set, clear): session-wide answers to ambiguities (merged under each request's args.assume)\n- reset(): drop every definition (the process image is restarted)\n- schema(): this interface as JSON Schema\n- funcs(): every defined function\n- models(): the cost models\n- use(model*): make a cost model active\n- help(): the command summary\nEvery op also takes assume (answers to ambiguities, from an error's readings), defaults, timeout_s, files.  Example: {\"op\": \"define\", \"args\": {\"f\": \"x^3 - 3x\"}}", "inputSchema": {"type": "object", "properties": {"op": {"type": "string", "enum": ["define", "state", "assume", "reset", "schema", "funcs", "models", "use", "help"], "description": "the operation"}, "args": {"type": "object", "description": "the op's named arguments (see the description; the exact schema of each op is in the session tool's schema op)"}}, "required": ["op"], "additionalProperties": false}, "outputSchema": {"type": "object", "required": ["id", "ok", "cmd"], "properties": {"id": {"description": "the request's id, as given (null if none)"}, "ok": {"type": "boolean"}, "cmd": {"type": ["string", "null"]}, "ucas": {"description": "the ucas statements that ran (error positions refer to them)", "type": "string"}, "structured": {"description": "result has fields beyond text", "type": "boolean"}, "result": {"description": "the command's fields (kind, ...); exact values as {value, exact}; expressions as ucas strings that parse back; unstructured commands give {text}", "type": "object"}, "results": {"description": "every result, when the request ran several commands", "type": "array"}, "notes": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"enum": ["rule", "info", "assumed", "default"]}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}}, "conditions": {"description": "where the answer holds", "type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}}, "checks": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"type": "string"}, "points": {"type": "integer"}, "max_diff": {"type": "number"}, "passed": {"type": "boolean"}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}}, "proof": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"enum": ["symbolic", "exhaustive", "sat", "numeric", "search"]}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}, "files": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"name": {"type": "string"}, "mime": {"type": "string"}, "bytes": {"type": "integer"}, "path": {"type": "string"}, "base64": {"type": "string"}}}}, "text": {"description": "the output as the CLI prints it", "type": "string"}, "error": {"type": "object", "required": ["code", "message"], "properties": {"code": {"enum": ["bad_json", "bad_request", "unknown_command", "parse_error", "domain_error", "unsupported", "failed", "ambiguous", "needs_input", "not_understood", "timeout", "internal"]}, "message": {"type": "string"}, "pos": {"type": "object", "properties": {"line": {"type": "integer"}, "col": {"type": "integer"}}}, "key": {"description": "ambiguous: the args.assume key that picks a reading", "type": "string"}, "readings": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"index": {"type": "integer"}, "reading": {"type": "string"}, "default": {"type": "boolean"}, "how": {"type": "string"}}}}, "how": {"type": "string"}}}}}}, {"name": "homological", "title": "Homological algebra", "description": "Exact homology and cohomology of spaces (spheres, tori, RP^n, CP^n, Klein bottle, lens spaces L(m,q), products, wedges, suspensions, simplicial or cellular complexes you give) with any f.g. abelian coefficients; long exact sequences with the snake lemma; the Bockstein spectral sequence (pages, d_r, E_inf), element tracing, and the check of bockstein.pdf's Proposition 0.1.  Every claim carries its checks (d o d = 0, exactness, well-defined induced maps, universal coefficients).\n\nCall with {\"op\": OP, \"args\": {...}}; expressions are ucas syntax strings (x^2 sin(x), isqrt(x: u4)) or an AST ({\"op\": \"+\", \"args\": [...]}).  Ops (* = required arg):\n- space(space*, unreduced): a cell complex: its cells, Euler characteristic and boundaries (d o d = 0 checked)\n- homology(space*, unreduced, coefficients, generators): H_n(X; G) for every n, exactly, with the universal coefficient theorem as a check\n- cohomology(space*, unreduced, coefficients, generators): H^n(X; G) for every n, exactly, with both universal coefficient theorems as checks\n- les(space*, unreduced, modulus*): the long exact sequence of 0 -> C -m-> C -> C (x) Z/m -> 0 on cochains, the connecting map by the snake lemma, exactness verified at every spot\n- bockstein(space*, unreduced, p*, pages): the Bockstein spectral sequence: pages E_r, D_r and d_r of the exact couple of 0 -> C -p-> C -> C (x) Z/p -> 0, derived exactly until stable\n- bockstein_trace(space*, unreduced, p*, degree*, element, page): trace a in H^n(X; Z) through the Bockstein spectral sequence: j_r(p^(r-1) a) in E_r, in ker d_r?, in im d_r? (with a preimage)\n- prop01(space*, unreduced, p*, pages): check Proposition 0.1 of bockstein.pdf on a space: for a generating a Z summand of H^n(X; Z), j_r(p^(r-1) a) is in ker d_r and not in im d_r, for every n and every r (all r up to the stable page, which covers the rest)\nEvery op also takes assume (answers to ambiguities, from an error's readings), defaults, timeout_s, files.  Example: {\"op\": \"space\", \"args\": {\"f\": \"x^3 - 3x\"}}", "inputSchema": {"type": "object", "properties": {"op": {"type": "string", "enum": ["space", "homology", "cohomology", "les", "bockstein", "bockstein_trace", "prop01"], "description": "the operation"}, "args": {"type": "object", "description": "the op's named arguments (see the description; the exact schema of each op is in the session tool's schema op)"}}, "required": ["op"], "additionalProperties": false}, "outputSchema": {"type": "object", "required": ["id", "ok", "cmd"], "properties": {"id": {"description": "the request's id, as given (null if none)"}, "ok": {"type": "boolean"}, "cmd": {"type": ["string", "null"]}, "ucas": {"description": "the ucas statements that ran (error positions refer to them)", "type": "string"}, "structured": {"description": "result has fields beyond text", "type": "boolean"}, "result": {"description": "the command's fields (kind, ...); exact values as {value, exact}; expressions as ucas strings that parse back; unstructured commands give {text}", "type": "object"}, "results": {"description": "every result, when the request ran several commands", "type": "array"}, "notes": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"enum": ["rule", "info", "assumed", "default"]}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}}, "conditions": {"description": "where the answer holds", "type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}}, "checks": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"type": "string"}, "points": {"type": "integer"}, "max_diff": {"type": "number"}, "passed": {"type": "boolean"}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}}, "proof": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"enum": ["symbolic", "exhaustive", "sat", "numeric", "search"]}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}, "files": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"name": {"type": "string"}, "mime": {"type": "string"}, "bytes": {"type": "integer"}, "path": {"type": "string"}, "base64": {"type": "string"}}}}, "text": {"description": "the output as the CLI prints it", "type": "string"}, "error": {"type": "object", "required": ["code", "message"], "properties": {"code": {"enum": ["bad_json", "bad_request", "unknown_command", "parse_error", "domain_error", "unsupported", "failed", "ambiguous", "needs_input", "not_understood", "timeout", "internal"]}, "message": {"type": "string"}, "pos": {"type": "object", "properties": {"line": {"type": "integer"}, "col": {"type": "integer"}}}, "key": {"description": "ambiguous: the args.assume key that picks a reading", "type": "string"}, "readings": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"index": {"type": "integer"}, "reading": {"type": "string"}, "default": {"type": "boolean"}, "how": {"type": "string"}}}}, "how": {"type": "string"}}}}}}, {"name": "proofs", "title": "Proofs", "description": "An LCF proof kernel for abstract algebra: state theorems (theorem), prove them (prove: the library's proofs, replays, automation for linear integer arithmetic, abelian-group equalities, subgroup membership and diagram chases; on failure a counterexample from concrete Bockstein spectral sequences), print the proof tree and its axioms (proof), re-check with an independent checker (proof_check).  The library proves bockstein.pdf's Proposition 0.1 for all complexes, primes, n and r, two ways (theorem bockstein: ...; prove bockstein).\n\nCall with {\"op\": OP, \"args\": {...}}; expressions are ucas syntax strings (x^2 sin(x), isqrt(x: u4)) or an AST ({\"op\": \"+\", \"args\": [...]}).  Ops (* = required arg):\n- theorem(name*, statement*): state a theorem in the kernel's language (forall x:el, n:int: ..., and or not -> <->, = <= <, in; the library's sorts, functions and predicates: see lemmas and axioms)\n- prove(name*, using): prove a stated theorem: by the library's proofs of the same statement (every route, each re-checked independently), else by replaying the library's proofs and by automation; when it fails, a counterexample is searched in concrete Bockstein spectral sequences\n- proof(name*): print a proved theorem's proof: each route's script, the tree of lemmas it rests on with their kernel inferences, and the axioms used\n- proof_check(name*): re-check a proved theorem with the independent checker (kcheck.c)\n- axioms(name): the axioms of the proof library (definitions and the integer arithmetic of Z); with a name, the ones that theorem's proofs rest on\n- lemmas(): the proof library's lemmas and theorems\nEvery op also takes assume (answers to ambiguities, from an error's readings), defaults, timeout_s, files.  Example: {\"op\": \"theorem\", \"args\": {\"f\": \"x^3 - 3x\"}}", "inputSchema": {"type": "object", "properties": {"op": {"type": "string", "enum": ["theorem", "prove", "proof", "proof_check", "axioms", "lemmas"], "description": "the operation"}, "args": {"type": "object", "description": "the op's named arguments (see the description; the exact schema of each op is in the session tool's schema op)"}}, "required": ["op"], "additionalProperties": false}, "outputSchema": {"type": "object", "required": ["id", "ok", "cmd"], "properties": {"id": {"description": "the request's id, as given (null if none)"}, "ok": {"type": "boolean"}, "cmd": {"type": ["string", "null"]}, "ucas": {"description": "the ucas statements that ran (error positions refer to them)", "type": "string"}, "structured": {"description": "result has fields beyond text", "type": "boolean"}, "result": {"description": "the command's fields (kind, ...); exact values as {value, exact}; expressions as ucas strings that parse back; unstructured commands give {text}", "type": "object"}, "results": {"description": "every result, when the request ran several commands", "type": "array"}, "notes": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"enum": ["rule", "info", "assumed", "default"]}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}}, "conditions": {"description": "where the answer holds", "type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}}, "checks": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"type": "string"}, "points": {"type": "integer"}, "max_diff": {"type": "number"}, "passed": {"type": "boolean"}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}}, "proof": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"enum": ["symbolic", "exhaustive", "sat", "numeric", "search"]}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}, "files": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"name": {"type": "string"}, "mime": {"type": "string"}, "bytes": {"type": "integer"}, "path": {"type": "string"}, "base64": {"type": "string"}}}}, "text": {"description": "the output as the CLI prints it", "type": "string"}, "error": {"type": "object", "required": ["code", "message"], "properties": {"code": {"enum": ["bad_json", "bad_request", "unknown_command", "parse_error", "domain_error", "unsupported", "failed", "ambiguous", "needs_input", "not_understood", "timeout", "internal"]}, "message": {"type": "string"}, "pos": {"type": "object", "properties": {"line": {"type": "integer"}, "col": {"type": "integer"}}}, "key": {"description": "ambiguous: the args.assume key that picks a reading", "type": "string"}, "readings": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"index": {"type": "integer"}, "reading": {"type": "string"}, "default": {"type": "boolean"}, "how": {"type": "string"}}}}, "how": {"type": "string"}}}}}}, {"name": "ucas", "description": "raw ucas statements (the escape hatch).  Any ucas statements, as typed at the ucas> prompt, e.g. \"f(x: u8) = x*x\\nrange f\" or \"x[0] = 1; x[k+1] = 2x[k]\"", "inputSchema": {"type": "object", "properties": {"source": {"type": "string", "description": "ucas source; several lines allowed"}, "code": {"type": "string", "description": "a code block for the statement (SPIR-V assembly or GLSL)"}, "assume": {"type": "object", "description": "answers to ambiguities: {key: reading or index}, e.g. {\"caret\": \"power\", \"z\": \"complex\"}"}, "defaults": {"type": "boolean", "description": "take the default reading of every ambiguity (as the CLI does with a note) instead of an error"}, "timeout_s": {"$ref": "#/$defs/number", "description": "wall-clock limit; the request runs in a forked child and the state is unchanged on a timeout"}, "files": {"enum": ["write", "base64", "both", "none"], "description": "what to do with files: write (to --dir, default), base64 (inline, nothing written), both, none"}, "answers": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}, "description": "replies to follow-up questions, in order"}}, "required": ["source"], "additionalProperties": false, "$defs": {"number": {"description": "a JSON number, or a constant expression in ucas syntax (\"pi/2\", \"inf\")", "type": ["number", "string"]}}}, "outputSchema": {"type": "object", "required": ["id", "ok", "cmd"], "properties": {"id": {"description": "the request's id, as given (null if none)"}, "ok": {"type": "boolean"}, "cmd": {"type": ["string", "null"]}, "ucas": {"description": "the ucas statements that ran (error positions refer to them)", "type": "string"}, "structured": {"description": "result has fields beyond text", "type": "boolean"}, "result": {"description": "the command's fields (kind, ...); exact values as {value, exact}; expressions as ucas strings that parse back; unstructured commands give {text}", "type": "object"}, "results": {"description": "every result, when the request ran several commands", "type": "array"}, "notes": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"enum": ["rule", "info", "assumed", "default"]}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}}, "conditions": {"description": "where the answer holds", "type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}}, "checks": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"type": "string"}, "points": {"type": "integer"}, "max_diff": {"type": "number"}, "passed": {"type": "boolean"}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}}, "proof": {"type": "object", "properties": {"kind": {"enum": ["symbolic", "exhaustive", "sat", "numeric", "search"]}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}, "files": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"name": {"type