{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 14, "result": {"prompts": [{"name": "cheaper_implementation", "description": "Find and prove a cheaper implementation of a function on its machine types", "arguments": [{"name": "f", "description": "the function, with types: \"days(m: u8 in 1..12) = match m { 2 => 28, 4 | 6 | 9 | 11 => 30, _ => 31 }\" or isqrt(x: u4)", "required": true}]}, {"name": "prove_identity", "description": "Prove (or refute with a counterexample) that two expressions are equal", "arguments": [{"name": "identity", "description": "the claimed identity, e.g. sin(x)^2 + cos(x)^2 = 1 or (x: u8) * 2 = x << 1", "required": true}]}, {"name": "explore_function", "description": "Study a function: its properties, critical points, integral and a plot", "arguments": [{"name": "f", "description": "the function, e.g. x^3 - 3x or sin(x)/x", "required": true}]}]}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 15, "result": {"description": "Find and prove a cheaper implementation of a function on its machine types", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": {"type": "text", "text": "Use the ucas tools to find a cheaper implementation of isqrt(x: u4).  Define it with session/define (typed parameters), then: analyze range and wrap (what it computes, where it overflows), analyze cost (under the active GPU model), analyze find (cheaper equivalent implementations, verified on the whole domain) and, for up to 6 input bits, analyze gates (a minimal gate network with a proof).  Confirm the best candidate with analyze equiv and report it with its cost and the proof each tool gave."}}]}}
